    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609-a3">

                <pb facs="0748" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg640"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Quincy to Mr. Merrill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    No. 20, of the 28th ultimo, relative to certain landed property in Jerusalem
                    owned by one Hyman J. Roos, who claimed to be an American citizen, I have to
                    state that this Department is in receipt of his certificate of naturalization
                    and that his name appears to be Hyman Rose, and not Hyman J. Roos, as given in
                    his letter of March 23 last.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josiah Quincy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
